# gnupg -- the gpg binary itself, and the last recipe before gpgme.
#
# THIS PACKAGE EXISTS FOR ONE REASON: gpgme does not implement crypto. It spawns
# gpg and drives it over Assuan, and flatpak takes gpgme as a hard dependency
# with no option guard. Every flatpak install verifies a GPG signature on the
# ostree summary, and this is the program that does it.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://gnupg.org/ftp/gcrypt/gnupg/gnupg-2.4.8.tar.bz2
SRC_SHA256=b58c80d79b04d3243ff49c1c3fc6b5f83138eb3784689563bcdd060595318616
SRC_DIR=gnupg-2.4.8

# --disable-tofu IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS, AND IT IS A TIME BOMB RATHER THAN A
# PREFERENCE.
#
# TOFU is ENABLED BY DEFAULT (configure sets use_tofu=yes) and needs sqlite3.
# sqlite3 is not packaged today, and configure DOES NOT FAIL when it is missing
# -- it reaches line 9488 and sets use_tofu=no. So without this flag the build
# succeeds and TOFU is quietly absent, and whether gpg has a TOFU trust model
# becomes a property of whatever happened to be installed.
#
# THAT IS NOT HYPOTHETICAL HERE. sqlite3 is already in this workstream's own
# queue: libsoup requires it, libsoup is required by gnome-software, and
# gnome-software is the end of this same chain. So sqlite3 WILL be packaged, and
# on the next rebuild after it lands an unnamed --disable-tofu would silently
# flip gnupg from no-TOFU to TOFU -- a different binary, a different trust model,
# no recipe change, and nothing reporting it.
# Naming it pins the outcome across that event. Flatpak signature verification
# does not use TOFU; it checks a detached signature against a key already in the
# keyring.
#
# COMPONENTS TURNED OFF, each because it is out of scope for signature
# verification and each of which would otherwise be built:
#   --disable-gpgsm      S/MIME. Not used by flatpak or ostree.
#   --disable-scdaemon   smartcard daemon; wants pcsc-lite or libusb at run time.
#   --disable-tpm2d      needs a TPM2 TSS stack that is not packaged.
#   --disable-wks-tools  Web Key Service tooling; needs a mail path to be useful.
#   --disable-doc        texinfo IS packaged and the docs would build; off to save
#                        time rather than because it would fail.
#
# KEPT ON DELIBERATELY, recorded because trimming them is the obvious next step
# for someone making this smaller:
#   dirmngr and keyboxd stay. dirmngr is where gpg's network access lives, and
#   NEITHER ntbtls NOR gnutls IS PACKAGED, so it builds without TLS and hkps
#   keyserver access is simply absent -- which is correct here, because nothing
#   in this distribution fetches keys from a keyserver. flatpak imports the
#   Flathub key from the .flatpakrepo file directly. Disabling dirmngr entirely
#   would work today and would make gpg behave unlike gpg everywhere else, for
#   no gain.
#
# EVERY --disable-gpg-<algorithm> IS LEFT ALONE, and that is the same reasoning
# as libgcrypt's CPU features one level down. configure offers to remove RSA,
# ECDH, ECDSA, EdDSA, CAST5, BLOWFISH, TWOFISH, IDEA, the AES sizes, the
# CAMELLIA sizes, MD5, RMD160 and the SHA variants. Removing an algorithm from a
# VERIFIER does not harden it -- it makes it unable to check signatures that were
# made with that algorithm, and this program's entire job here is checking
# signatures made by other people years ago with choices we do not control.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --disable-doc --disable-tofu \
--disable-gpgsm --disable-scdaemon --disable-tpm2d --disable-wks-tools"
